WEBVTT

00:00:04.201 --> 00:00:05.577
Hmm.

00:00:07.499 --> 00:00:09.501
Horsie to pointy guy six.

00:00:17.931 --> 00:00:18.927
Check.

00:00:18.952 --> 00:00:19.998
Hmm.

00:00:20.589 --> 00:00:21.590
Get 'im, boys.

00:00:25.642 --> 00:00:26.810
Good move.

00:00:58.533 --> 00:01:00.118
Good news, everyone.

00:01:00.202 --> 00:01:01.244
We have a mission

00:01:01.328 --> 00:01:04.873
to further the noble cause
of intergalactic peace.

00:01:04.957 --> 00:01:06.333
Nope. Watching cartoons.

00:01:06.416 --> 00:01:07.542
Sorry.

00:01:08.418 --> 00:01:09.670
What's the mission?

00:01:09.753 --> 00:01:12.965
It's a delivery for
the Democratic Order of Planets.

00:01:13.048 --> 00:01:14.299
"DOOP"? What's that?

00:01:14.383 --> 00:01:17.469
It's similar to the United Nations
from your time, Fry.

00:01:17.552 --> 00:01:18.595
Uh...

00:01:18.679 --> 00:01:21.598
Or like the Federation
from your Star Trek program.

00:01:21.765 --> 00:01:22.808
Oh!

00:01:22.891 --> 00:01:26.395
Tonight is the ribbon cutting
for the DOOP's new headquarters.

00:01:26.478 --> 00:01:27.521
What are we delivering?

00:01:27.604 --> 00:01:31.066
Something without which
no ribbon-cutting ceremony could proceed,

00:01:31.149 --> 00:01:34.111
the ceremonial oversized scissors.

00:01:34.194 --> 00:01:36.613
We'll get them there as quickly as we can.

00:01:36.697 --> 00:01:38.949
All right, but don't run with them.

00:01:46.164 --> 00:01:47.249
Wow!

00:01:47.332 --> 00:01:48.792
There's a million aliens.

00:01:48.875 --> 00:01:50.961
I've never seen anything so mind-blowing.

00:01:51.461 --> 00:01:54.506
Ooh! A reception table with muffins!

00:01:55.257 --> 00:01:56.675
Ladies and gentlemen,

00:01:56.758 --> 00:01:58.760
welcome to the ribbon-cutting ceremony

00:01:58.844 --> 00:02:01.513
of the DOOP's
magnificent new headquarters,

00:02:01.596 --> 00:02:03.974
a fitting home for an organization

00:02:04.057 --> 00:02:06.768
that has fostered peace
throughout the universe.

00:02:06.852 --> 00:02:10.105
Even between the Insectoids
and the Space Lizards.

00:02:15.902 --> 00:02:18.697
So, what's it like on Planet Amazonia?

00:02:18.780 --> 00:02:19.948
Big rats there.

00:02:20.032 --> 00:02:21.700
Me crush with club.

00:02:21.783 --> 00:02:23.702
That's so interesting.

00:02:23.785 --> 00:02:26.371
Maybe we could get to know
each other over a coffee.

00:02:26.455 --> 00:02:29.750
I can think of no better place
for this center of diplomacy

00:02:29.833 --> 00:02:32.836
than here in orbit
around the Neutral Planet.

00:02:32.919 --> 00:02:34.129
What are your thoughts

00:02:34.212 --> 00:02:36.632
on this momentous occasion,
Your Neutralness?

00:02:36.715 --> 00:02:40.177
I have no strong feelings
one way or the other.

00:02:41.928 --> 00:02:44.514
I hate these filthy Neutrals, Kif.

00:02:44.598 --> 00:02:46.308
With enemies, you know where they stand.

00:02:46.391 --> 00:02:47.893
But with Neutrals, who knows?

00:02:47.976 --> 00:02:49.728
It sickens me.

00:02:51.438 --> 00:02:52.439
Halt!

00:02:52.522 --> 00:02:54.024
Why, Leela,

00:02:54.107 --> 00:02:56.485
I do believe we've met.

00:02:56.568 --> 00:02:58.236
He means you guys did it.

00:02:58.320 --> 00:03:02.115
If you don't mind, we're here to deliver
the scissors for the ribbon cutting.

00:03:02.199 --> 00:03:04.868
- Then you're under arrest.
- What for?

00:03:04.952 --> 00:03:08.372
How do I know these scissors
aren't part of some Neutral plot?

00:03:08.455 --> 00:03:09.957
But they're not even sharp.

00:03:10.040 --> 00:03:11.875
Who could I possibly hurt with them?

00:03:11.959 --> 00:03:14.586
The Yarn People of Nylar IV.

00:03:16.672 --> 00:03:21.176
So, a plan to assassinate
a weird-looking alien with scissors.

00:03:21.259 --> 00:03:23.053
How very neutral of you.

00:03:23.136 --> 00:03:24.262
What?

00:03:24.346 --> 00:03:28.016
It was almost the perfect crime,
but you forgot one thing.

00:03:28.100 --> 00:03:30.644
Rock crushes scissors.

00:03:31.103 --> 00:03:35.065
But paper covers rock.
And scissors cuts paper.

00:03:35.148 --> 00:03:37.693
Kif, we have a conundrum.

00:03:37.776 --> 00:03:40.612
Search them for paper.
And bring me a rock.

00:03:40.696 --> 00:03:41.697
Why?

00:03:41.780 --> 00:03:43.073
So beautiful.

00:03:43.156 --> 00:03:44.950
Yet so neutral.

00:03:46.785 --> 00:03:48.203
Drag them to the ship.

00:03:48.287 --> 00:03:50.247
And now, to cut the ribbon,

00:03:50.330 --> 00:03:52.833
the legendary DOOP captain
who just returned

00:03:52.916 --> 00:03:55.794
from a triumphant carpet bombing
of Eden 7,

00:03:55.877 --> 00:03:57.671
Zapp Brannigan.

00:04:05.345 --> 00:04:08.265
What makes a man turn neutral?

00:04:08.348 --> 00:04:10.684
Lust for gold? Power?

00:04:10.767 --> 00:04:14.021
Or were you just born
with a heart full of neutrality?

00:04:14.104 --> 00:04:15.105
Sir...

00:04:15.188 --> 00:04:17.649
You're supposed to be
cutting the ribbon right now.

00:04:17.733 --> 00:04:19.610
No matter. I'll simply cut it from here

00:04:19.693 --> 00:04:20.902
with the ship's laser.

00:04:25.073 --> 00:04:27.242
Sir, I don't think that's wise.

00:04:27.326 --> 00:04:29.620
Kif, if there's one thing I don't need,

00:04:29.703 --> 00:04:32.414
it's your "I don't think
that's wise" attitude.

00:04:56.813 --> 00:04:58.523
Whoopsie-daisy.

00:05:02.402 --> 00:05:04.529
Zapp Brannigan, you stand accused

00:05:04.613 --> 00:05:06.448
of blowing up DOOP headquarters.

00:05:06.531 --> 00:05:07.783
How do you plead?

00:05:07.866 --> 00:05:10.786
Absolutely 99% not guilty.

00:05:10.869 --> 00:05:12.913
Then the prosecutor
will call his first witness.

00:05:12.996 --> 00:05:14.206
Your Honor,

00:05:14.289 --> 00:05:16.333
I'm just a simple hyper-chicken

00:05:16.416 --> 00:05:18.543
from a backwoods asteroid,

00:05:18.627 --> 00:05:23.423
but if it please the court
I reckon I'll call the entire jury.

00:05:26.510 --> 00:05:28.261
I'm going to allow this.

00:05:28.345 --> 00:05:30.222
Members of the jury,

00:05:30.305 --> 00:05:32.099
did y'all happen to catch a gander

00:05:32.182 --> 00:05:35.185
at who blew up
that there DOOP headquarters?

00:05:35.269 --> 00:05:36.478
That's the guy right there.

00:05:36.561 --> 00:05:38.021
- Right over there.
- Yes, indeed.

00:05:38.105 --> 00:05:40.941
And are y'all going to vote
to convict him?

00:05:41.066 --> 00:05:42.693
- Absolutely.
- You better believe it.

00:05:43.277 --> 00:05:46.363
The jury is instructed
to disregard its own testimony.

00:05:46.446 --> 00:05:48.907
Your Honor, the prosecution rests.

00:05:50.701 --> 00:05:53.203
The evidence against
Zapp Brannigan is strong.

00:05:53.287 --> 00:05:55.664
However, in light of his years of service

00:05:55.747 --> 00:05:58.458
and the incompetence
of this hillbilly prosecutor,

00:05:58.542 --> 00:06:00.961
I'm afraid I must dismiss all charges.

00:06:02.170 --> 00:06:03.964
Dismiss all charges?

00:06:04.047 --> 00:06:07.551
Your Honor, I know the case is closed
and you've rendered your verdict

00:06:07.634 --> 00:06:09.177
but I want to testify.

00:06:09.261 --> 00:06:11.054
I'm going to allow this.

00:06:11.138 --> 00:06:14.182
Now, Ms. Leela, on the date in question

00:06:14.266 --> 00:06:18.103
were you or were you not
wearing a hoopskirt?

00:06:18.186 --> 00:06:19.896
That's a stupid question.

00:06:19.980 --> 00:06:24.192
What matters is Zapp Brannigan
is the sorriest captain I've ever seen,

00:06:24.276 --> 00:06:27.362
and I saw the idiot blow up
DOOP Headquarters with my own eye.

00:06:29.323 --> 00:06:32.034
I'd like to cross-examine the witness.

00:06:32.117 --> 00:06:33.619
I'm going to allow this.

00:06:33.994 --> 00:06:36.830
- We've met before, have we not?
- Yes.

00:06:36.913 --> 00:06:40.667
And on that occasion,
did you have sex with someone?

00:06:40.751 --> 00:06:43.503
May I remind you,
you are still under oath.

00:06:43.712 --> 00:06:45.756
Yes.

00:06:45.839 --> 00:06:49.968
Please point out the person
in this courtroom you had sex with.

00:06:52.220 --> 00:06:53.472
Whoo!

00:06:54.431 --> 00:06:58.352
- And his name is?
- Zapp Brannigan.

00:06:58.435 --> 00:07:02.689
The very same Zapp Brannigan
who did not blow up DOOP Headquarters.

00:07:02.773 --> 00:07:04.775
I rest my case.

00:07:05.859 --> 00:07:09.488
Ladies and gentlemen of the jury,
you may begin your deliberations.

00:07:22.209 --> 00:07:25.045
Your Honor, we have reached a verdict.

00:07:25.128 --> 00:07:28.715
We find the defendant guilty.

00:07:28.966 --> 00:07:30.592
Whoo!

00:07:31.009 --> 00:07:32.177
Zapp Brannigan,

00:07:32.260 --> 00:07:34.596
you are hereby stripped
of your rank as captain

00:07:34.680 --> 00:07:36.556
and dismissed from the DOOP.

00:07:50.696 --> 00:07:53.991
I'd like to make one final statement.

00:07:54.074 --> 00:07:55.701
Kif, come here and hold up the flag.

00:07:57.494 --> 00:07:59.955
And wave it a little, for God's sakes.

00:08:00.038 --> 00:08:04.501
My friends, you can take away
a man's title and his uniform,

00:08:04.584 --> 00:08:08.213
but you can never take away
his integrity or his honor.

00:08:08.297 --> 00:08:11.216
- Plus, it was mostly Kif's fault.
- What?

00:08:11.300 --> 00:08:14.469
Kif Kroker, you are also
stripped of your rank

00:08:14.553 --> 00:08:16.179
and dishonorably discharged.

00:08:24.271 --> 00:08:26.398
One day a man has everything,

00:08:26.481 --> 00:08:30.027
and the next day he blows up
a $400-billion space station,

00:08:30.110 --> 00:08:31.862
and the next day he has nothing.

00:08:31.945 --> 00:08:33.530
It makes you think.

00:08:33.614 --> 00:08:34.615
No, it doesn't.

00:08:34.698 --> 00:08:38.452
Come, Kif. It's time to begin
our life as civilians.

00:08:39.453 --> 00:08:40.954
That's an order, soldier.

00:08:47.461 --> 00:08:50.797
Everybody's talkin' at me

00:08:50.881 --> 00:08:54.968
I don't hear a word they're saying

00:08:56.219 --> 00:09:00.349
Only the echoes of my mind

00:09:03.894 --> 00:09:05.896
People stop and stare

00:09:07.564 --> 00:09:11.026
I can't see their faces

00:09:11.109 --> 00:09:13.779
Only the shadows

00:09:13.862 --> 00:09:15.405
Of their eyes

00:09:18.617 --> 00:09:22.496
I'm going where the sun
keeps shining...

00:09:22.579 --> 00:09:25.165
Through the pouring rain

00:09:27.042 --> 00:09:28.085
Hey, Bender?

00:09:28.168 --> 00:09:29.169
Yeah?

00:09:32.381 --> 00:09:33.423
All right.

00:09:33.507 --> 00:09:36.051
This is the third hose fight
I've broken up today,

00:09:36.134 --> 00:09:38.762
and the second one using actual hoses.

00:09:38.845 --> 00:09:39.972
Now move your lazy asses

00:09:40.055 --> 00:09:42.432
and start scrubbing the ship
like I ordered you to.

00:09:42.516 --> 00:09:45.060
You don't have to get so mad, Leela.

00:09:45.143 --> 00:09:48.480
Yeah, Fry already wiped off
some of the dirt with his finger.

00:09:54.987 --> 00:09:56.113
Zapp?

00:09:56.196 --> 00:09:58.699
Leela, I didn't know where else to turn.

00:09:58.782 --> 00:10:00.450
You're the only woman who ever loved me.

00:10:00.534 --> 00:10:01.827
I never loved you.

00:10:01.910 --> 00:10:04.204
- I mean physically.
- What do you want?

00:10:04.288 --> 00:10:06.039
Just let me work for a little food.

00:10:06.123 --> 00:10:07.749
Perhaps I could paint a fence,

00:10:07.833 --> 00:10:10.085
or service you sexually,
or mop the floors.

00:10:10.168 --> 00:10:12.587
You don't know how to do
any of those things.

00:10:12.671 --> 00:10:13.672
Kif might.

00:10:15.465 --> 00:10:16.967
Leela, who are you talking to?

00:10:17.050 --> 00:10:19.803
Just a broken-down hobo
who's hit rock bottom

00:10:19.886 --> 00:10:21.763
and his commanding officer.

00:10:21.847 --> 00:10:24.641
Why, you're that
disgraced starship captain.

00:10:24.725 --> 00:10:28.854
Having him on staff would distract people
from our horrendous safety record.

00:10:28.937 --> 00:10:30.314
Come in.

00:10:30.397 --> 00:10:33.275
I'd like everyone to meet
our new employees.

00:10:34.276 --> 00:10:35.319
Which ones are new?

00:10:35.402 --> 00:10:37.696
The green dude and the fat man.

00:10:37.779 --> 00:10:41.658
I could swear I've never seen
that robot before, either.

00:10:41.742 --> 00:10:42.993
I'm Bender.

00:10:43.076 --> 00:10:44.953
You know, the lovable rascal.

00:10:45.037 --> 00:10:48.957
Oh, yes, yes, my good friend, of course.

00:10:50.375 --> 00:10:51.376
Anyway,

00:10:51.460 --> 00:10:54.004
whoever you all are, I have good news.

00:10:54.087 --> 00:10:57.382
You'll be making a delivery to Stumbos IV,

00:10:57.466 --> 00:11:00.802
a planet with such high gravity,
you'll most likely be crushed

00:11:00.886 --> 00:11:02.721
under the weight of your own hair.

00:11:03.263 --> 00:11:04.598
Enjoy!

00:11:09.686 --> 00:11:11.229
So, this Leela,

00:11:11.313 --> 00:11:13.607
I know she's a very sensuous woman,

00:11:13.690 --> 00:11:15.484
but what manner of captain is she?

00:11:15.567 --> 00:11:17.611
- She's really strict.
- And mean.

00:11:17.694 --> 00:11:18.695
I see.

00:11:18.779 --> 00:11:21.657
Does she, by any chance,
give the crew members spankings?

00:11:21.740 --> 00:11:23.825
No, she just makes us do work and stuff.

00:11:23.909 --> 00:11:25.118
Good, good.

00:11:25.202 --> 00:11:29.414
But should she ever institute
some sort of bare-bottom spanking policy,

00:11:29.498 --> 00:11:30.874
let me go in your place.

00:11:30.958 --> 00:11:33.502
I won't have my comrades harmed.

00:11:33.585 --> 00:11:35.545
Hey, this guy's all right.

00:11:37.339 --> 00:11:40.133
Here's to us poor schmoes,

00:11:40.217 --> 00:11:41.593
working for the man.

00:11:41.677 --> 00:11:44.763
Even if he is a hot, sexy, female man.

00:11:50.519 --> 00:11:52.896
I've computed our landing
coordinates, Captain.

00:11:52.980 --> 00:11:54.856
Thanks, Kif. Very nice work.

00:11:55.691 --> 00:11:56.775
Wait. What?

00:11:56.858 --> 00:11:59.319
I said, "Very nice work."

00:11:59.403 --> 00:12:02.781
This is the happiest day of my life.

00:12:08.495 --> 00:12:10.080
Okay, crew, listen up.

00:12:10.163 --> 00:12:13.875
Your job is to deliver
these 40 pillows to that hotel.

00:12:13.959 --> 00:12:15.210
They're not very heavy,

00:12:15.294 --> 00:12:17.129
but you don't hear me not complaining.

00:12:17.212 --> 00:12:20.173
They're not heavy in here
because we have an anti-grav pump.

00:12:20.257 --> 00:12:23.969
But once you get out on the surface
the gravity will be very intense.

00:12:24.052 --> 00:12:25.178
Hey, no prob.

00:12:25.262 --> 00:12:27.139
This lead apron will protect me.

00:12:28.015 --> 00:12:29.683
I don't want any screwups.

00:12:29.766 --> 00:12:31.101
Use the hover dolly

00:12:31.184 --> 00:12:33.145
and just deliver one pillow at a time.

00:12:35.188 --> 00:12:36.481
Hey, here's an idea.

00:12:36.565 --> 00:12:38.609
Let's deliver all the pillows at once.

00:12:38.692 --> 00:12:41.445
- Yeah.
- That's using the old noodle.

00:12:50.704 --> 00:12:52.414
Come on, girdle.

00:12:52.497 --> 00:12:53.790
Hold.

00:12:57.294 --> 00:12:58.503
Uh-oh.

00:13:01.965 --> 00:13:03.550
What the hell happened?

00:13:03.634 --> 00:13:05.093
Some breaking occurred.

00:13:05.177 --> 00:13:07.596
The dolly was involved.
That's about all we know.

00:13:07.679 --> 00:13:10.807
I told you dumb apes not to overload it.

00:13:10.891 --> 00:13:13.810
Each of those pillows
weighs 150 pounds here.

00:13:13.894 --> 00:13:15.938
All right, don't get your panties
in a knot.

00:13:16.021 --> 00:13:17.522
We'll just use the backup dolly.

00:13:17.606 --> 00:13:19.149
I'll start loading up the pillows.

00:13:19.232 --> 00:13:20.525
No way, jack.

00:13:20.609 --> 00:13:21.818
You disobeyed an order.

00:13:21.902 --> 00:13:24.947
So now you have to deliver
all 40 pillows by hand.

00:13:25.614 --> 00:13:27.908
Let me ask you a serious question, Leela.

00:13:27.991 --> 00:13:31.411
Does the company that made your bra
make a girdle as well?

00:13:31.495 --> 00:13:32.913
I ask because a friend of mine...

00:13:32.996 --> 00:13:34.122
Just get to work.

00:13:37.626 --> 00:13:39.836
"I'm Leela. Get to work."

00:13:39.920 --> 00:13:41.171
I agree.

00:13:41.254 --> 00:13:45.467
The point is it's just so humiliating
working for that man.

00:13:45.550 --> 00:13:50.597
Once, he actually ordered me
to shave his armpits

00:13:50.681 --> 00:13:52.641
while he was in the bathtub.

00:13:52.724 --> 00:13:54.101
So I said to him...

00:13:54.184 --> 00:13:58.021
You know, why don't we talk about
something besides Zapp for a while?

00:13:58.105 --> 00:13:59.731
Oh, all right.

00:13:59.856 --> 00:14:01.149
Um...

00:14:01.233 --> 00:14:05.279
Well, how about them... Okay.

00:14:05.362 --> 00:14:07.406
Well, there he was in the tub, all right?

00:14:14.830 --> 00:14:17.165
Some good, old high-gravity rain.

00:14:17.249 --> 00:14:18.625
That'll cool us off.

00:14:25.382 --> 00:14:27.134
This is all Leela's fault.

00:14:27.217 --> 00:14:29.845
Yeah. If she had let us
use the backup dolly,

00:14:29.928 --> 00:14:32.681
we could have broken it, given up,
and gone home by now.

00:14:32.764 --> 00:14:36.018
You know, boys,
a good captain needs many skills

00:14:36.101 --> 00:14:39.646
such as boldness, daring
and a velour uniform.

00:14:39.730 --> 00:14:43.191
And I'm not convinced
Leela has any of those things.

00:14:43.358 --> 00:14:45.402
Ah. Leela's not that bad.

00:14:45.485 --> 00:14:47.529
I just wish she didn't
make us work so much.

00:14:47.613 --> 00:14:48.864
Back when I was captain

00:14:48.947 --> 00:14:51.867
all I asked from my men
was their complete loyalty.

00:14:51.950 --> 00:14:55.245
If I had that, then for all I cared
they could sit around the whole day

00:14:55.329 --> 00:14:57.581
drinking beer in their underpants.

00:14:57.664 --> 00:14:58.665
Beer?

00:14:58.749 --> 00:15:00.125
Underpants?

00:15:00.208 --> 00:15:01.501
Hmm.

00:15:01.835 --> 00:15:04.504
But now, Zapp's not captain anymore.

00:15:04.588 --> 00:15:06.131
I'm free.

00:15:06.840 --> 00:15:09.343
You hear that? I'm actually laughing.

00:15:09.426 --> 00:15:10.677
This is a mutiny.

00:15:11.845 --> 00:15:13.347
You're out of here, lady.

00:15:13.430 --> 00:15:15.015
Zapp's the new captain.

00:15:17.476 --> 00:15:19.770
All hail the new captain.

00:15:27.444 --> 00:15:30.614
Leela, you may be
a formidable doer of the nasty,

00:15:30.697 --> 00:15:32.783
but I am forced
to relieve you of your post.

00:15:32.866 --> 00:15:34.993
On what grounds, you slobbering oaf?

00:15:35.077 --> 00:15:37.204
Failure to prevent a mutiny.

00:15:37.454 --> 00:15:38.830
Throw her in the brig.

00:15:38.914 --> 00:15:39.957
We don't have a brig.

00:15:40.040 --> 00:15:41.750
Then throw her in the laundry room,

00:15:41.833 --> 00:15:44.503
which will hereafter
be referred to as the brig.

00:15:47.047 --> 00:15:49.299
You really don't want me
to be captain anymore?

00:15:49.383 --> 00:15:50.634
You got it, genius.

00:15:50.717 --> 00:15:52.928
But didn't I do a good job?

00:15:53.011 --> 00:15:54.680
You were mean, and you yelled,

00:15:54.763 --> 00:15:56.515
and you made us do all that work.

00:15:56.598 --> 00:15:59.101
Sometimes, a captain
needs to do those things.

00:15:59.184 --> 00:16:01.520
Besides, I thought we were friends.

00:16:01.603 --> 00:16:02.646
Yeah, well,

00:16:02.729 --> 00:16:05.524
you shouldn't have been
such a mean captain, then.

00:16:06.358 --> 00:16:07.609
Don't worry, Leela.

00:16:07.693 --> 00:16:10.404
Soon, we'll be able to
look back on this and laugh.

00:16:16.326 --> 00:16:18.829
Back in my old uniform.

00:16:18.912 --> 00:16:20.455
And it nearly still fits

00:16:20.539 --> 00:16:22.916
Even after all that
fattening hobo cuisine.

00:16:23.000 --> 00:16:26.003
What shall I do with
your civilian clothes, sir?

00:16:26.086 --> 00:16:27.754
Take them to the laundry brig.

00:16:28.255 --> 00:16:30.257
So, do I have your loyalty, men?

00:16:30.340 --> 00:16:32.092
To the ends of the universe.

00:16:32.175 --> 00:16:33.552
Ten-hundred percent.

00:16:33.635 --> 00:16:35.679
That's not nearly loyal enough.

00:16:35.762 --> 00:16:39.808
I order you to sit around and drink beer
until you're as loyal as Kif here.

00:16:40.267 --> 00:16:41.768
Yes, sir, sir.

00:16:42.561 --> 00:16:43.979
May I have a beer, sir?

00:16:44.062 --> 00:16:46.481
No, you're loyal enough already.

00:16:46.565 --> 00:16:48.066
Meanwhile, I have a plan.

00:16:48.150 --> 00:16:52.404
We will single-handedly attack
our archenemy, the Neutral Planet.

00:16:52.487 --> 00:16:53.572
Oh, geez.

00:16:53.655 --> 00:16:55.991
Once the Neutral War Machine
lies in ruins,

00:16:56.074 --> 00:16:57.492
I'll be a hero again

00:16:57.576 --> 00:17:00.329
and the DOOP will reinstate me as captain.

00:17:00.412 --> 00:17:03.707
But, sir, that plan makes no sense.

00:17:03.790 --> 00:17:05.000
Maybe not to you, Kif.

00:17:05.083 --> 00:17:06.418
But if I recall correctly,

00:17:06.501 --> 00:17:09.087
you were court-martialed in disgrace.

00:17:09.379 --> 00:17:10.714
Ooh! Burn.

00:17:10.797 --> 00:17:12.215
Nailed you, buddy.

00:17:16.887 --> 00:17:20.515
Prepare to continue the epic struggle
between good and neutral.

00:17:20.599 --> 00:17:21.767
This is awesome.

00:17:21.892 --> 00:17:23.602
We're going to be like... Pow, pow, pow!

00:17:23.685 --> 00:17:25.020
And they're going to be like...

00:17:27.022 --> 00:17:30.233
And then, we'll have pancakes
to celebrate, and I'll be like...

00:17:31.485 --> 00:17:32.653
Precisely.

00:17:32.736 --> 00:17:35.906
Now, in the name of all
that is good and honorable,

00:17:35.989 --> 00:17:38.659
we'll call the Neutral president
with a message of peace,

00:17:38.742 --> 00:17:39.952
then blast him.

00:17:40.035 --> 00:17:42.829
Yes, sir, sirdy, sir, sir, sir.

00:17:42.913 --> 00:17:45.374
Fly the white flag of war.

00:17:51.797 --> 00:17:55.759
This is Zapp Brannigan of the good ship...
Planet Express ship.

00:17:55.842 --> 00:17:58.345
I come swinging the olive branch of peace.

00:17:58.428 --> 00:18:00.138
Should we trust him, Your Neutralness?

00:18:00.222 --> 00:18:03.517
All I know is, my gut says, "Maybe."

00:18:05.435 --> 00:18:07.145
What now, chief?

00:18:07.229 --> 00:18:09.189
Now, we crash the ship
into their headquarters,

00:18:09.273 --> 00:18:13.777
killing them in a hellish firestorm
from which no living thing can escape.

00:18:13.860 --> 00:18:15.612
Good, good. Then what?

00:18:15.696 --> 00:18:17.322
Then your mission is complete.

00:18:17.406 --> 00:18:21.618
I, meanwhile, will have ejected to safety
wearing the only space suit on board.

00:18:26.039 --> 00:18:28.292
Wait a second.
Is this plan going to kill us?

00:18:28.375 --> 00:18:29.459
Of course.

00:18:29.543 --> 00:18:31.461
What do you think I meant by loyalty?

00:18:31.545 --> 00:18:33.630
Now, help me into the only space suit.

00:18:33.714 --> 00:18:35.007
It looks a bit sweaty in there

00:18:35.090 --> 00:18:37.384
so you may need to apply baby powder.

00:18:39.428 --> 00:18:41.763
Leela, we want you to be captain again.

00:18:41.847 --> 00:18:42.973
Let me guess,

00:18:43.056 --> 00:18:44.516
he canceled nap time?

00:18:45.392 --> 00:18:46.560
He ran out of beer?

00:18:47.227 --> 00:18:48.895
So he's about to kill us.

00:18:50.480 --> 00:18:53.025
We want Leela to be captain again.

00:18:53.108 --> 00:18:54.526
So, it's mutiny, is it?

00:18:54.610 --> 00:18:56.695
I never thought I'd see the day.

00:18:56.778 --> 00:18:58.238
Come, Kif, let's eject.

00:18:58.322 --> 00:19:00.324
I found a children's space suit
you can wear.

00:19:00.407 --> 00:19:01.825
Well, to be honest, sir,

00:19:01.908 --> 00:19:03.827
I'd rather stay here with Captain Leela.

00:19:03.910 --> 00:19:06.413
She actually listens to what I have to...

00:19:19.092 --> 00:19:21.845
Oh, no. He's disabled the steering.

00:19:22.512 --> 00:19:23.805
We're gonna crash!

00:19:23.889 --> 00:19:25.182
Leela, save me.

00:19:25.849 --> 00:19:27.351
And yourself, I guess.

00:19:27.434 --> 00:19:29.102
And my banjo.

00:19:30.562 --> 00:19:32.105
And Fry.

00:19:32.189 --> 00:19:33.732
Okay, okay.

00:19:33.815 --> 00:19:35.025
We have one chance.

00:19:35.108 --> 00:19:37.194
Are you willing to do
what I say as captain?

00:19:37.277 --> 00:19:39.738
- Absolutely.
- Even if I make you work hard?

00:19:39.821 --> 00:19:42.032
As your God is my witness.

00:19:42.115 --> 00:19:44.368
Then go get the hover dolly
you didn't break

00:19:44.451 --> 00:19:47.120
and load all the Dark Matter
into the left engine.

00:19:47.204 --> 00:19:49.456
Oh, man, that crap's heavy.

00:19:49.539 --> 00:19:51.541
- And warm.
- Just do it!

00:19:55.128 --> 00:19:57.547
Your Neutralness, it's a beige alert.

00:19:57.631 --> 00:19:59.091
If I don't survive,

00:19:59.174 --> 00:20:01.176
tell my wife, "Hello."

00:20:02.344 --> 00:20:03.345
Hurry!

00:20:03.428 --> 00:20:05.555
I don't want to die at the age of 25!

00:20:05.639 --> 00:20:09.268
Honey, unless we hit a time warp,
I wouldn't worry about it.

00:20:14.106 --> 00:20:15.816
- It's too low!
- Quick!

00:20:25.993 --> 00:20:28.662
You did it. You actually did it!

00:20:30.247 --> 00:20:32.833
And no one will have to
punish anyone for the mutiny.

00:20:37.546 --> 00:20:39.715
And so, when Captain Leela panicked,

00:20:39.798 --> 00:20:42.092
perhaps distracted by female troubles,

00:20:42.175 --> 00:20:45.637
my quick thinking allowed me
to do whatever I did to save the day.

00:20:45.721 --> 00:20:49.850
Captain Leela, is this rambling story
of magic and heroism true?

00:20:49.933 --> 00:20:52.269
- Well, actually...
- That-a-girl.

00:20:52.352 --> 00:20:55.397
If they don't take him back,
we can keep him as captain.

00:20:57.482 --> 00:20:58.775
Your Honor, it's all true.

00:20:58.859 --> 00:21:01.486
My female incompetence,
Zapp's catlike reflexes,

00:21:01.570 --> 00:21:03.905
the stuff that made no sense, all of it.

00:21:05.866 --> 00:21:07.743
In that case, Zapp Brannigan,

00:21:07.826 --> 00:21:11.371
I hereby restore your rank
and parking privileges.

00:21:15.083 --> 00:21:16.627
Oh, foo.

00:21:16.752 --> 00:21:18.629
Come, Kif. We've got work to do.

00:21:21.048 --> 00:21:22.090
Oh.

00:21:22.591 --> 00:21:24.343
I'll call and tell you about it.

00:21:24.426 --> 00:21:25.552
Oh.

00:21:29.765 --> 00:21:32.768
Leela, I just want you to know
that even though you're mean,

00:21:32.851 --> 00:21:34.686
you're the best captain ever.

00:21:34.770 --> 00:21:37.356
Yeah, you're one dynamite lady.

00:21:37.439 --> 00:21:39.650
- Can we have the week off?
- No.

00:21:39.733 --> 00:21:41.109
Please?

00:21:41.193 --> 00:21:42.986
Come on, Captain.

00:21:43.070 --> 00:21:44.655
Oh, all right.

00:21:44.738 --> 00:21:46.823
No time off.

00:21:46.907 --> 00:21:48.241
Oh, man.

00:21:48.325 --> 00:21:49.618
Let's mutiny.